(b) C1-type two-band face-touching construction (1D, beta=m=1):
    lower band = exact SLAC E0=sqrt(1+k^2) on the zone; partner = tower band 1, sqrt(1+(2pi-rho(k))^2),
    capped smoothly near k=0 (rho = |k| outside |k|<w).  Analytic branch B (partner) on the zone:
    w=1.00: int(u_B'') = -6.28322 (pred -2pi=-6.28319); mean anomaly (u_B''-1) = -2.0000; min u_B'' = -5.8; partner >= lower: True
    w=0.30: int(u_B'') = -6.28322 (pred -2pi=-6.28319); mean anomaly (u_B''-1) = -2.0000; min u_B'' = -20.4; partner >= lower: True
    w=0.10: int(u_B'') = -6.28322 (pred -2pi=-6.28319); mean anomaly (u_B''-1) = -2.0000; min u_B'' = -62.3; partner >= lower: True
    w=0.03: int(u_B'') = -6.28322 (pred -2pi=-6.28319); mean anomaly (u_B''-1) = -2.0000; min u_B'' = -208.9; partner >= lower: True
    -> the partner carries a fixed anomaly -2 (zone mean), independent of the cap; it sits at E ~ sqrt(1+4pi^2) = 6.362

(c) truncated tower with N analytic branches glued into one 2*pi*N-periodic branch U(kappa) (1D):
    paraboloid U = (1+kappa^2)/2 on |kappa| < pi*N - w, smooth turn at the top; total anomaly int(U''-1):
    N=  1: int(U''-1) =   -6.2831  (pred -2piN =   -6.2832), located at E ~ 3.3
